# Marketplace maintainers own tooling, config, workflows, schemas, and docs by
# default - anything not matched by a more specific rule below.
* @bcgov/agent-marketplace-maintainers

# Community namespaces are intentionally ownerless (a path listed with no owner
# removes the default owner). Eligible community submissions publish on the
# automated intake gate (.github/workflows/community-intake.yml), not human
# review, so they must not require a CODEOWNERS approval. This covers every
# supported extension type.
/skills/community/
/prompts/community/
/instructions/community/
/agents/community/
/hooks/community/
/mcp/community/

# Specialty namespaces require the owning team's review before merge - for ANY
# extension type. The namespace is the second path segment
# (<type>/<specialty>/<name>/). Add a line per specialty as it comes online.
/skills/security/ @bcgov/security
/prompts/security/ @bcgov/security
/instructions/security/ @bcgov/security
/agents/security/ @bcgov/security
/hooks/security/ @bcgov/security
/mcp/security/ @bcgov/security

